                "text": "Strategy: Meteor Strikes are the same in terms of strength as their nuclear missile counterpart but has a higher attack range. The other differences is they do not need any uranium to be developed or needed to research the Manhattan Project. With these in mind, you can now use all of your uranium resources over the construction of other needed buildings and units.Historical Info: Before meteors became the fiery balls falling from the sky that we know, they are initially known as asteroids. Asteroids are a chunk of rocks that can be found orbiting a celestial body, from planets to stars. These rocks can vary in size, they can be as small as a grain of sand and can be as big as the size of a mountain. Within the Alverez theory, it suggests that a meteor once struck Earth, theoretically  the same size as Mt. Everest, causing a massive explosion of an estimated amount of 100,000,000 megatonnes of TNT exploding all at once, this theory is also known to theorize one of the possible causes of the Cretaceous-Paleogene Mass Extinction Event. Within the Advance Wars series, Sturm is notoriously known for his ability to pull meteors near the planet's orbit, crushing down the armies of his foes."
            }
        ]
    },

