        "promotions": ["[Han Chu-Ko-Nu] ability"],
        "civilopediaText": [
            {
                "text": "The chu-ko-nu was a repeating crossbow that first emerged during the Warring States period, between the fifth and third centuries BCE. Its magazine was attached to the top of the weapon and could hold up to twenty bolts at a time. A single pull of its handle drew the drawstring, dropped the bolt in place, and sent the projectile flying. Some models could fire two bolts at a time. The chu-ko-nu's mechanism enabled its rate of fire to far surpass hand-drawn bows and standard crossbows; it was also extremely easy to use, making it a weapon of choice for civilians who lacked military training. However, the chu-ko-nu was not particularly powerful; given that bolts often failed to fatally pierce their targets, they were sometimes tipped with poison to ensure victims met an untimely end."
