                "text": "Songhai was a highly effective conquest-oriented empire in the Sahel region of West Africa. It took over territory from the Malian Empire and formed a key node in Muslim networks spanning the Sahara. The Songhai military was based around several axes: a riverine navy, a cavalry, and a highly-trained infantry known for the gold bangles they wore on their arms. \nThis reliance on medieval warfare based around swords and lances was their undoing. Even by the time of Askia the Great, in 1493, the tides were turning. Guns had entered the battlefield, so it was only a matter of time before a foreign force realized that Songhai lands were ripe for the taking. In 1591, Morocco delivered this blow, and the better-equipped Arab forces seized control of Songhai’s salt and gold resources."
